// BidClearing — handles the auction.
// Interface sketch; implementation lands with the Compact toolchain.
//
// placeBid(
//     brandId,
//     amountUsd,
//     slot
// )
//
// clearBid(
//     bidId,
//     aggregateProof
// )
//
// Clearing semantics: a bid does NOT clear on the first correct answer.
// `aggregateProof` is a single proof attesting that the segment's attention
// threshold was met across the full attention window — not one proof per
// listener. Individual submitAttentionProof calls accumulate private state;
// clearBid consumes the aggregate.
// Flow: BID -> AD PLAYS -> ATTENTION WINDOW -> VALID ATTENTION EVENTS
//       -> THRESHOLD MET? -> CLEARING (full bid) -> REWARD POOL CREATED.
// If the threshold isn't met, the bid does not clear. The advertiser buys a
// defined slot of verified attention that either clears or doesn't.
